    <string name="help_title">About the app</string>
    <string name="help_about">Erebuni 782 — a trilingual (hy/ru/en) offline guide to the Urartian fortresses Erebuni (782 BC) and Teishebaini (Karmir Blur). Works without internet.</string>
    <string name="help_tourist_title">Tourist mode</string>
    <string name="help_tourist_body">Guide: fortress cards open articles. Wiki: mini-encyclopedia about kings, gods, daily life. Library: books (PDF reader, font size, night mode, bookmarks) and audio (Urartu.fm station, your music). Map: fortress coordinates. Settings: switch language and skin on the fly.</string>
    <string name="help_employee_title">Employee mode</string>
    <string name="help_employee_body">Protected by PIN (set once, change later). Registry of artifacts with categories, photos, custody status, audit log, inspection reminders. Aerial survey: stitch photos, tap to mark objects, auto-detect anomalies at 3 sensitivity levels, generate 3D reconstruction by era. Export signed .e782 file for PC or device-to-device sync.</string>
    <string name="help_fm_title">Urartu.fm</string>
    <string name="help_fm_body">Offline station with owner\'s soundtrack (10 melodies). Play/pause from the top bar or Library → Audio. Toggle off if you don\'t like it.</string>
    <string name="map_image_desc">Stylized map showing Erebuni and Teishebaini fortresses near Yerevan</string>
    <string name="map_walk_title">How to get there on foot</string>
    <string name="map_drive_title">How to get there by car</string>
    <string name="map_open_maps">Open map</string>
    <string name="map_navigate">Navigate</string>
    <string name="map_erebuni_walk">From Yerevan center: take bus 16 or trolleybus 2 to Arin-Berd stop (south-east, ~20 min). Walk uphill 300 m following signs to the museum entrance.</string>
    <string name="map_erebuni_drive">From Republic Square: head south on Vardanants St, turn right onto Artashat Hwy, continue 4 km, turn left at Arin-Berd sign, follow the road uphill to the museum parking.</string>
    <string name="map_teishebaini_walk">From Yerevan center: take bus 5 or 32 to Karmir Blur stop (west, ~15 min). The excavated citadel is visible from the main road, 200 m walk north.</string>
    <string name="map_teishebaini_drive">From Republic Square: head west on Tigran Mets Ave, cross the Hrazdan bridge, continue on Erebuni Hwy 2.5 km, turn right at Karmir Blur sign.</string>
    <string name="map_disclaimer">Offline map illustration. Tap «Open map» or «Navigate» to launch your maps app with GPS coordinates.</string>
